<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $105 mln Dec 4.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $105 mln Dec 4.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $105 million surplus on December 4 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 4</p>
<p>Exports: $185.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $140.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $201.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $142.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $105 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $605.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $483.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $617.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $394.8 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $344.6 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
